# Create a clear structure

<h2 id="put-the-most-important-thing-first">Put the most important thing first</h2>

Start with what the person needs most. Use headings that say what the section is for.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Introduction | Check the hallway motion sensor |

<h2 id="use-lists-for-steps">Use numbered lists for steps</h2>

Use a numbered list when the order matters.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Check the battery, then move the sensor closer, then restart it. | 1. Check the battery.<br>2. Move the sensor closer.<br>3. Restart the sensor. |

<h2 id="wg-050">Order instructions around the task</h2>

Put the step first, then the reason. Give one action per step and say what the person should see.

<%= example('wg-instructions') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| You may want to consider opening the lamp’s settings to rename it. | 1. Open the lamp’s settings. The name field appears.<br>2. Enter the new name.<br>3. Save it. The lamp shows the new name. |

<h2 id="wg-051">State real prerequisites and consequences</h2>

Before a step, say what must be true. Before a risky step, say what will happen. For risks to people, see [Write a warning](states-and-errors.html#wg-042).

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Restore the backup. | Restoring a backup replaces your current settings. Changes made since the backup was taken are lost. |

<h2 id="wg-052">Refer to the actual interface</h2>

Use the label shown on screen. Write “select”, not “click”.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Click the cog, then disable the automation. | Select **Settings**, then **Automations & scenes**. Turn off **Porch light at sunset**. |

<h2 id="wg-054">Ask only what you need</h2>

Every question must change what happens next. Mark optional questions.

<%= example('wg-form-purpose') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Alert settings | Alert when the front door opens after 10pm? (optional) Leave blank for no door alerts. |

<h2 id="wg-061">Ask for personal information only when needed</h2>

Say why you need it and what happens if it is left blank.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Enter your phone number. | Phone number (optional). Used only to text you when the alarm sounds. |
